A good script should handle errors.

Example:

#!/bin/bash

SOURCE="/home/bilal"
DEST="/backup"

if [ ! -d "$SOURCE" ]; then
    echo "Source directory does not exist"
    exit 1
fi

if [ ! -d "$DEST" ]; then
    echo "Backup directory does not exist"
    exit 1
fi

echo "Starting backup..."

Here:

exit 1

means the script exits with an error.
